course: dictionary
lesson: 3732
title: Floating ice
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A floe is a large, flat sheet of ice floating on the sea. Picture a giant frozen pancake drifting on the water. It is a noun, so one is a floe and more than one are floes.
explain: The context helps you find the meaning. «Orcas in Antarctica swim side by side to make a wave that washes a seal off an ice floe.» The seal is on the ice and the wave washes it off, so an ice floe must be a flat piece of ice that sits on the water and can hold a seal.
explain: Floes are pieces of sea ice, and they often drift, which means they are carried slowly along by the sea. Drifting floes are floes on the move. To check your meaning, swap in "a large flat sheet of floating ice" and see whether the sentence still makes sense. It does.
fact: A floe is a large, flat sheet of floating ice on the sea.
fact: An ice floe is a piece of sea ice that floats on the water.
fact: Polar bears hunt seals from floes, and seals rest on them.
fact: As the climate warms, there is less sea ice and fewer floes in summer.
fact: In stories, explorers sometimes drift on floes.
exercise: What is a floe? | *A large flat sheet of floating ice on the sea | A deep hole cut into a glacier | A small iceberg on a mountain lake
exercise: In «Orcas in Antarctica swim side by side to make a wave that washes a seal off an ice floe», what does the wave wash the seal off? | The side of the wave | Antarctica | *An ice floe | The orcas
exercise: Why are there fewer floes in summer now? | There is more snow on the sea in summer | Polar bears carry the floes inland | *As the climate warms, there is less sea ice | Seals have eaten the floes
test: Which phrase means floating ice carried along by the sea? | *Drifting floes | Dry land | Sandy beaches | Hot springs
test: Where do polar bears hunt seals? | In hot desert sand | High on mountain tops | *From ice floes | Under the sea bed
exam: Which meaning fits in «Explorers drifted for weeks on a floe»? | A hot drink made from milk | A tall tower of rock | A kind of fish | *A large flat sheet of floating ice
